s":"Unthemed","subtheme":"General – Financial Services - Micro-enterprise / MSME NBFC (small-ticket rural & semi-urban business loans, unsecured-to-secured transition)","tag":"General","theme":"Unclassified","tier":""}],"thesis":"FY26 was an explicitly self-described year of \"transition, correction and strengthening\" — Moneyboxx sacrificed growth to fix a book that got caught in the MFI-guardrail spillover, and the asset-quality repair is now visible and large: GNPA 6.61% → 3.59%, NNPA 3.42% → 1.75%, bucket-1/bucket-2 resolution rates at \"the highest level achieved by the company since inception\". The cost of that repair is that the P&L is barely above breakeven (FY26 PAT ₹1.34cr on ₹232cr total income) because opex (12.8%) is carried against a shrunken ₹893cr AUM. The FY27 thesis is entirely an operating-leverage bet: management has told its lenders a **43–44% AUM jump** and expects credit cost **below 2%**, to be delivered through a secured mix pivot (68% → target ~80% by Mar-27), FLDG/second-loss-backed partnership sourcing that carries no sales cost, and a new solar/renewable-asset product targeted at ~10% of AUM.","trig":[]},"lm":"","m":391,"mem":0,"pdd":"","prev_stage":1,"prev_zone_vpe":0.0,"r":null,"s":"MONEYBOXX","sig":"","sx":{"SMA_50":"61.1","base_count":"","drawdown_from_prev_signal":"","duration_from_prev_signal":"","pct_below_52w_high":"44.0","pct_change_from_prev_signal":"","pivot_close":"","pivot_low":"","stage_changed_since_prev_signal":"","vpe_df_60d_sum":"-0.1","vpe_zone_cumul_df":"-0.1"},"t":""}},"s":"MONEYBOXX"}